Veeco Instruments Inc., together with its subsidiaries, develops, manufactures, sells, and supports semiconductor and thin film process equipment primarily to make electronic devices in the United States, Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, China, Rest of the Asia-Pacific, and internationally. It offers laser annealing, ion beam deposition and etch, metal organic chemical vapor deposition, single wafer wet processing and surface preparation, molecular beam epitaxy, advanced packaging lithography, atomic layer deposition, and other deposition systems. The company's process equipment systems are used in the production of a range of microelectronic components, including logic, dynamic random-access memory, photonics devices, power electronics, radio frequency filters and amplifiers, magnetic heads for hard disk drives, and other semiconductor devices. In addition, it markets and sells its products to integrated device manufacturers and foundries; outsourced semiconductor assembly and test companies; and hard disk drive and photonics manufacturers, as well as research centers and universities. Veeco Instruments Inc. was founded in 1945 and is headquartered in Plainview, New York.","ceo_bio":"Dr. William John Miller Ph.D. | CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $693,694 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $525K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Each employee generates $42K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $29K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Veeco Instruments Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $2.4B market cap on $664M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, with gross margins sitting at 40%.","The business throws off $53M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 8 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.96\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 3.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.2% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 102% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.0244103555498},{"text":"Operating margins softening -1.6pp YoY \u2014 early warning on the moat","sev":"amber","cat":"trend"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $27.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 12% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"What Veeco Instruments (VECO) Earnings Guidance Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-veco/veeco-instruments/news/what-veeco-instruments-veco-earnings-guidance-means-for-shar","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794617635.239,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.477,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Veeco Instruments (VECO) Could Be 30% Undervalued On Q3 Results And Fresh Guidance","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/semiconductors/nasdaq-veco/veeco-instruments/news/veeco-instruments-veco-could-be-30-undervalued-on-q3-results","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794475925.154,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.931,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Veeco Instruments (NASDAQ:VECO) Cut to Buy at Wall Street Zen","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/10/veeco-instruments-nasdaqveco-cut-to-buy-at-wall-street-zen.html","date":"2026-11-10","timestamp":1794292978.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"Veeco Instruments Inc. $VECO Stock: ProShare Advisors LLC Decrease